          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An alternative to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+topological+vector+spaces"} complete topological vector spaces
            in the framework of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+mathematics"} condensed mathematics
          %p
            Roughly, completeness is expressed as ability to integrate with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measures"} Radon measures
          %p
            This doesn’t quite work as stated, and to make this rigorous one has to bring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L%5Ep-spaces"} L^p-spaces
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi p
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\lt p\le 1
            (i.e., the non-convex case) into the picture.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+abelian+group"} condensed abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              \-liquid
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi p
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\lt p\le 1
            ) if for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+topological+space"} compact Hausdorff topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and every morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
